  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WFP HUM 2022-2025</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">WFP HUM 2022-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Aktuell insats avser Sidas bidrag av medel till FN:s livsmedelsprogram (WFP) med anledning av akut livsmedelsotrygghet i l&#xe4;nder s&#xe5;som Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Burkina Faso, Centralafrikanska republiken, Demokratiska republiken Kongo, El Salvador, Etiopien, Guatemala, Guinea, Haiti, Honduras, Jemen, Kamerun, Kenya, Madagaskar, Mali, Mauretanien, Mo&#xe7;ambique, Myanmar, Niger, Nigeria, Palestina, Somalia, Sudan, Sydsudan, Syrien, Tchad, Uganda, Ukraina, Venezuela och Zambia.

St&#xf6;det omfattar totalt 2 050 500 000 kronor under avtalsperioden, inklusive 422 500 000 kronor f&#xf6;r att n&#xe5; krisdrabbade m&#xe4;nniskor i 14 l&#xe4;nder under 2025.

Insatsen innefattar &#xe4;ven st&#xf6;d till FN:s humanit&#xe4;ra flygtj&#xe4;nst (UNHAS) i syfte att m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;ra tilltr&#xe4;de f&#xf6;r humanit&#xe4;ra akt&#xf6;rer till m&#xe4;nniskor i behov av humanit&#xe4;rt st&#xf6;d i omr&#xe5;den som inte &#xe4;r tillg&#xe4;ngliga genom andra l&#xf6;sningar.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The current contribution provides Sida funding to the World Food Programme (WFP) to support the organisation&#x2019;s humanitarian response to acute food insecurity in countries such as Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Burkina Faso, Cameroon, Central African Republic, Chad, Democratic Republic of the Congo, El Salvador, Ethiopia, Guatemala, Guinea, Haiti, Honduras, Kenya, Madagascar, Mali, Mauritania, Mozambique, Myanmar, Niger, Nigeria, Palestine, Somalia, Sudan, South Sudan, Syria, Uganda, Ukraine, Venezuela and Zambia.

The support amounts to a total of SEK 2,050,500,000 over the agreement period, including SEK 422,500,000 to reach crisis-affected populations in 14 countries in 2025.

The intervention also includes support to the United Nations Humanitarian Air Service (UNHAS) to facilitate access for humanitarian actors to people in need of assistance in areas that cannot be reached by other means.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WFP is Sida&apos;s main partner for responding to food needs in humanitarian settings, and has proven to be a highly effective partner in providing the assistance and protection to the most affected populations. WFP&apos;s capacity has been strengthened through the reform process which the organization underwent during the previous agreement period.

Sida will contribute funds to WFP to respond to the humanitarian needs of affected populations during 2022, within two main categories: a) Crisis response through food, nutrition and resilience assistance  and b) enhanced access through UNHAS.</narrative>
  </description>
